## [Serverless logic tier](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/serverless-logic-tier.md)

### [AWS Lambda](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/aws-lambda.md)

AWS Lambda is a compute service that enables you to run arbitrary code functions without provisioning, managing, or scaling servers.

- [Your business logic goes here, no servers necessary](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/your-business-logic-goes-here-no-servers-necessary.md): Lambda requires you to write code functions, called handlers, which will run when initiated by an event.
- [Lambda security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/lambda-security.md): To run a Lambda function, it must be invoked by an event or service that is permitted by an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policy.
- [Performance at scale](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/performance-at-scale.md): Code pulled in as a container image from Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), or from a zip file uploaded to Amazon S3, runs in an isolated environment managed by AWS.
- [Serverless deployment and management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/serverless-deployment-and-management.md): To help you deploy and manage your Lambda functions, use AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM), an open-source framework that includes:

### [Amazon API Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/amazon-api-gateway.md)

Amazon API Gateway is a fully managed service that enables developers to create, publish, maintain, monitor, and secure APIs at any scale.

- [Integration with AWS Lambda](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/integration-with-aws-lambda.md): Amazon API Gateway supports both REST and HTTP types of APIs.
- [Stable API Performance Across Regions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/stable-api-performance-across-regions.md): Each deployment of Amazon API Gateway includes a Amazon CloudFront distribution under the hood.
- [Encourage innovation and reduce overhead with built-in features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/encourage-innovation-and-reduce-overhead-with-built-in-features.md): The development cost to build any new application is an investment.

### [Iterate rapidly, stay agile](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/iterate-rapidly-stay-agile.md)

Using Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda to build the logic tier of your API enables you to quickly adapt to the changing demands of your user base by simplifying API deployment and version management.

- [Prioritize API security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/prioritize-api-security.md): All applications must ensure that only authorized clients have access to their API resources.


## [Data tier](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/data-tier.md)

- [Serverless data storage options](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/serverless-data-storage-options.md): Amazon S3 is an object storage service that offers industry-leading scalability, data availability, security, and performance.
- [Non-serverless data storage options](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/serverless-multi-tier-architectures-api-gateway-lambda/non-serverless-data-storage-options.md): Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) is a managed web service that makes it easier to set up, operate, and scale a relational database using any of the available engines (Amazon Aurora, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, Oracle, and Microsoft SQL Server) and running on several different database instance types that are optimized for memory, performance, or I/O.


